CHANGES RELATIVE TO EMWM 2.1
----------------------------

Removed:

  * The backdrop subsystem (WmBackdrop.c/.h) and all associated resources.
    EMWM mapped a full-screen, override-redirect window over the root window
    of every workspace, which permanently hid anything drawn on the root by
    xsetroot(1), feh(1), hsetroot(1) or xwallpaper(1). mWizard does not create
    that window, so those tools work normally.

  * X Session Management Protocol support (WmXSMP.c/.h), which only did
    anything when an external session manager was running, together with the
    client resource database it maintained.

  * The _MWM_WM_REQUEST root-window property protocol (WmRequest.c/.h), which
    existed so that a separate helper program could drive workspaces from
    outside. Its functionality is available directly as rc-file functions.

  * The "standard behavior" mode (useStandardBehavior) and the four duplicate
    resource tables that supported it.

  * Code guarded by preprocessor macros that no makefile defined:
    MOTIF_ONE_DOT_ONE, HP_VUE, DESKTOP, WSM, OLD_CODE, NOTDONE, PORT_OLDXLIB,
    SGI_FOCUS_PATCH, ICCC_COMPLIANT, FIX_1193, NO_MESSAGE_CATALOG and the
    OPEN LOOK compatibility layer (WmOL.h).

  * The cppCommand resource, which was wired to a preprocessing routine that
    was already compiled out.

Added:

  * An internal session facility (WmSession.c/.h) providing f.logout,
    f.reboot, f.shutdown and f.suspend, each backed by a user-configurable
    command so that mWizard has no hard dependency on systemd or any other
    particular service manager. An optional idle-lock timer runs a
    user-provided locker such as xscreensaver or i3lock.

  * f.rename_workspace, replacing the NAMWKSPC request of the removed
    property protocol.

  * An extended rc-file format (WmSettings.c/.h) with Settings and Client
    blocks, so that window manager behaviour is configured in one file
    instead of being split between the rc file and the X resource database.
    The X resource database now carries appearance settings only.

Unchanged on purpose:

  * X atom names. _MOTIF_WM_HINTS, _MWM_WM_HINTS, _MWM_WORKSPACE_*, WM_STATE,
    WM_PROTOCOLS and the _NET_* set are the interoperability contract that
    Motif and other toolkits rely on. Renaming them would break every client
    that speaks them, so mWizard keeps them exactly as EMWM had them.
